{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": false,
    "declaration": true,
    "declarationMap": true,
    "sourceMap": true,
    "outDir": "./dist",
    "rootDir": "./src"
    /* Resolution stays `bundler` (inherited). That is what lets the package
       import `@blobbi-kit/core/color-guardrails` — an `exports`-map subpath
       that classic `node` resolution cannot see.
       CONSEQUENCE, and a recorded publication blocker: the emitted JS keeps
       extensionless relative specifiers (`from './svg'`), which every bundler
       resolves and bare Node ESM does not. Publishing to npm for Node
       consumers needs an extension-rewriting step (tsup/rollup) added here
       first — see the package README, "Publication status". */
  },
  "include": ["src"],
  "exclude": ["src/**/*.test.ts", "src/**/*.test.tsx"]
}
